[size=6][b]Asgard Build Limiter[/b][/size]

[i]The art of ATF shipbuilding is fading. Replacement Asgards take time - or never come.[/i]

This mod puts a configurable construction delay on Terran AI Asgard building. When the Protectorate takes up an Asgard order, the work takes time - and you will hear about it: a logbook rumour reports that Terran engineers are trying to revive an ancient ATF battleship design. Set the delay high enough, and the lost art stays lost.

Player-owned shipyards are unaffected, and player-built Asgards are never delayed. Self-imposed handicaps are left to the player; this mod only limits NPC Terran faction AI.

[size=4][b]Why[/b][/size]

In vanilla, losing an Asgard costs the Terran Protectorate about one minute of paperwork: the job system orders a replacement the moment the wreck cools, for less metallic microlattice than a Syn. For a ship lore says nobody remembers how to build - and that no other faction can answer - that is neither balanced nor believable.

[size=4][b]Game version compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][i] 9.00 release[/i] - [b]supported[/b][/*]
[*][i] 9.00 betas and release candidates[/i] - [b]supported[/b][/*]
[*][i] 8.00 release[/i] - [b]supported[/b][/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Dependencies[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Cradle of Humanity DLC[/b] - the mod limits Terran Asgard production; without the DLC there is nothing to limit.[/*]
[*][b]SirNukes Mod Support APIs[/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/x4foundations/mods/503]link[/url]) - provides the Extension Options menu used for configuration.[/*]
[/list]

Both are hard dependencies. The mod will not load without them.

[size=4][b]What it does[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Intercepts the Terran job system's Asgard build orders and holds them until the configured cooldown since the last Asgard build has elapsed.[/*]
[*]Touches nothing else: escorts, Syns, destroyers and the rest of the Terran war machine build normally. Fleets simply wait for their flagship.[/*]
[*]Your own shipyards are unaffected - this limits the AI faction only.[/*]
[/list]

The held build occupies no shipyard slot, no resources and no build queue; the job just retries later, exactly as it would if a shipyard were unavailable.

[size=4][b]Configuration[/b][/size]

Extension Options -> Asgard Build Limiter:

[list]
[*][b]Enabled[/b] - default: on. Turn the limiter off to restore vanilla behaviour.[/*]
[*][b]Cooldown[/b] - default: 120 min. In-game minutes between AI Asgard builds.[/*]
[/list]

Guide: 60-120 minutes makes Asgards a rare, punishing loss instead of a disposable asset. Crank the slider to maximum and the Terrans will effectively never field a new one - the art is lost for good.

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Patches two spots in vanilla [font=Courier New]md/job_helper.xml[/font]; no other vanilla files touched. Safe to add to or remove from an existing save.[/*]
[/list]

Pairs well with an Asgard main battery rebalance like [b]Asgard Spinal Lance Re-Balanced[/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/x4foundations/mods/869]link[/url]), if you believe a single ship out-gunning the rest of the galaxy fifty-fold was a typo.

